{
	title: 'hal/intro: a friendly first-run guide',
	spec: 'hal/intro (src/host/synthetic.ts) is the first-run guide, a synthetic model that asks with forms and acts on the answers (no provider needed). It walks, one question at a time, each skippable: 1) name, written to USER.md as "# User\\n\\nName: <name>\\n" (task n2; if USER.md already has a Name line it greets by it and skips the question); 2) optionally a sentence about what they mostly work on and how they like answers, appended to USER.md under "## About"; 3) provider login: when no account is logged in it explains and offers to start /login (the command, as if typed), else says which accounts exist; 4) the default model, offered only among listed models whose provider has a usable nonempty file account (accessToken or apiKey) or environment API key, applied like /model; if no such credential exists after login, skip the model step; 5) web search: it says that Hal searches the web with the google tool through Serper for every model (serper.dev; its free searches go a long way), and asks yes or no whether to set up Serper; on yes it asks for the API key in a secret field and stores it as serper.apiKey in the credentials file through the same liveFile path provider accounts use (task g6); skipped when a Serper key already exists; 6) it closes with three or four short tips (Escape pauses, Alt-Enter queues, /help, /keys, the web client address) and how to switch this tab to a real model. It is resumable: after a restart or a steered message it continues from the first step not yet answered, reading history (answer records) and USER.md, never asking twice. Writes to USER.md go through one small host function that creates the file with the header when missing and appends otherwise. A fresh home with no sessions opens its first tab on hal/intro. Tests: the steps in order with skips; USER.md content after name and about; an existing Name skips step 1; resuming mid-way; no login offers /login. Tests also cover an empty credential and filtering out unavailable providers even when the configured default is from one.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'hal/intro advances by named answer records and USER.md rather than a volatile step counter. The first tab alone starts on hal/intro; provider tests with preexisting homes must seed a provider session. Login launches the real slash command after the intro turn; Serper uses apiKeys.save/liveFile with 0600 and its secret answer never enters history.',
		'E2E provider tests must wait for the preexisting session’s first host socket and then the peer UI before sending commands; session count is nonzero before either process starts, so using it as readiness races and drops keystrokes.',
		'Keep model choices tied to the available credential provider IDs, not the configured default; an unconfigured default must not sneak into the options. If the login step is skipped with no credentials, go straight to search.'
